{"id":"5045d216c83e75cb","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-omega.md","title":"Natural Number Set","display":"df-omega — Natural Number Set","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-omega","aliases":["58-df-omega"],"display":"df-omega — Natural Number Set","depends_on":["[[58-ax-inf]]","[[58-df-emptyset]]","[[58-df-union]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-omega"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-omega</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-omega — Natural Number Set"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"828011acc1ee6ac5\" href=\"?note=828011acc1ee6ac5\" title=\"58-ax-inf\">58-ax-inf</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0b8de0824384672e\" href=\"?note=0b8de0824384672e\" title=\"58-df-emptyset\">58-df-emptyset</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5a295a90caf70085\" href=\"?note=5a295a90caf70085\" title=\"58-df-union\">58-df-union</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\emptyset\">\\(\\emptyset\\)</span> (empty set)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span> (defined here; set of natural numbers)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Inductive}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Inductive}_S\\)</span> (inductive-set predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Omega}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Omega}_S\\)</span> (natural-number-set predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}omega} \\vdash \\mathrm{Inductive}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\in I\\land\\forall x\\in I\\;(x\\cup\\{x\\}\\in I)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}omega} \\vdash \\mathrm{Inductive}_S(I)\\leftrightarrow \\emptyset\\in I\\land\\forall x\\in I\\;(x\\cup\\{x\\}\\in I)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}least\\text{-}inductive\\text{-}set} \\vdash \\mathrm{Omega}_S(W)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Inductive}_S(W)\\land\\forall I\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{Inductive}_S(I)\\to W\\subseteq I)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}least\\text{-}inductive\\text{-}set} \\vdash \\mathrm{Omega}_S(W)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Inductive}_S(W)\\land\\forall I\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{Inductive}_S(I)\\to W\\subseteq I)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}omega\\text{-}exists} \\vdash \\mathrm{Omega}_S(\\omega)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}omega\\text{-}exists} \\vdash \\mathrm{Omega}_S(\\omega)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The axiom of infinity supplies an inductive set; separation within such a witness yields the unique least inductive set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\">\\(\\omega\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The definition avoids taking an intersection over the proper class of all inductive sets.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-inf","status":"resolved","id":"828011acc1ee6ac5","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","locati